  "rationale": "Deploying mfa:admin alone blocks both auth_dc and auth_adfs. Those are the only ways to obtain the footholds needed for admin_dc or admin_adfs, which are required to steal database-admin credentials. Without those credentials, none of the database, fileserver, or backup exfiltration routes can proceed. With zero controls, an attack succeeds via phish_workstation → pivot_internal → auth_appserver → kerberoast_dc → auth_dc → escalate_dc → dump_dbadmin_dc → auth_db → escalate_db → exfiltrate_db. Therefore the minimum is exactly one control."
